A negative operand is read as the clause's value rather than as an unknown option, so the run
succeeds and every row with a numeric id passes `id:gt=-1`.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
vault_path: ./vault
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/p3/index.md --
---
id: 3
---

body
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/p5/index.md --
---
id: 5
---

body
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/p10/index.md --
---
id: 10
---

body
-- cmd --
booping query --glob 'plans/*/index.md' --where id:gt=-1 --output paths
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
plans/p10/index.md
plans/p3/index.md
plans/p5/index.md
